  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Dissolve ingredients (except sulfur, yeast extract, vitamins and sulfide), adjust pH to 3.5 with 10 N H2SO4 and sparge medium with 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture for 30 – 45 min to make it anoxic."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials (e.g., 20 ml medium in 100 ml bottles) containing already the appropriate amount of sulfur."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "Sterilize medium by heating cultivation vessels in a water bath to 90 – 100°C for 1 – 2 hours on each of 3 successive days."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "Add yeast extract, vitamins (sterilized by filtration) and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Adjust pH of complete medium to 4.0 - 4.5, if necessary."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "After inoculation pressurize vials to 1 bar overpressure with sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "Adjust pH of final solution to 2 with 1 N HCl."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}